{
  "dom_id": "step-q131400",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(Z\\ge -1.32).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0643\\,$ | $\\,0.0630\\,$ | $\\,0.0618\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0778\\,$ | $\\,0.0764\\,$ | $\\,0.0749\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0934\\,$ | $\\,0.0918\\,$ | $\\,0.0901\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge -1.32).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/d89bd5f38fdf4c952146dde8cd01207167c92cab07290742d229ceb0f4cf5712.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-P(Z<-1.32) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(-1.32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/0959a3c48bf70d10f24d85cd98bcd0703db4765ba5349d02896e18104c3f98a7.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\u03a6(-1.32)=0.0934.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge -1.32) & =1-\u03a6(-1.32) \\\\  & =1-0.0934 \\\\  & =0.9066.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
